      "content": "maintenance is gonna kill us right now. we've got that trans-pacific route scheduled for tonight and if we pull this bird, we're losing a massive amount of revenue and the whole schedule's gonna blow up. \n\nis it really that urgent? it's only at the very edge of the caution zone. can we just monitor it during the flight and deal with it once it's back on the ground? i need to know if this is a genuine safety risk or just some sensor noise/operational variance.",
